      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be a subject matter expert in innovation projects in various IT domains and will play an active role in the academic, professional & personal development of your learners to prepare them for work & life. [What you will be working on] Design, develop, and deliver engaging ICT‑related modules, including curriculum design, lesson facilitation, and assessment activities Guide and mentor students through applied learning, capstone projects, and industry‑relevant assignments Collaborate with industry partners to identify, initiate, and support real‑world projects, internships, or applied learning opportunities Continuously review and enhance curriculum content to keep pace with evolving technologies, industry trends, and workforce needs Participate in academic, professional, and student‑development activities to support the mission of the School of Information Technology [What we are looking for] At least 3 years’ experience in an ICT‑related role such as software development, systems engineering, cloud engineering, DevOps, cybersecurity, IT operations, solution architecture, or technical consultancy Academic or professional qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or a related discipline Industry certifications (e.g., Cloud, DevOps, Systems, or Platform‑related certifications) are an advantage but not mandatory Strong interest in applied learning, innovation, skills development, and continuous professional growth Ability to translate industry practices and technical concepts into meaningful learning experiences for students Experience working on or supporting IT projects, products, or platforms in a professional environment Familiarity with modern software development or IT delivery practices such as Agile, DevOps, or iterative delivery models Passion for working with youths and young adults, with an interest in mentoring, coaching, and developing future ICT professionals Experience in any of the following would be advantageous: Software development, scripting, or automation Cloud platforms and services (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP, or equivalent enterprise platforms) DevOps, CI/CD pipelines, or platform engineering Containerization or virtualization technologies Systems administration, networking, or infrastructure management Infrastructure‑as‑Code or configuration management tools Web platforms, application hosting, or distributed systems #LI-Hybrid"
