    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Adjunct-Lecturer---Parademic_JR-10000050883": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer - Paramedicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-27\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] This adjunct position offers an opportunity for practicing professionals to educate and mentor the next generation of paramedics on a flexible, part-time basis. As a subject matter expert, you will be responsible for delivering theoretical knowledge and practical skills across various diploma levels, ensuring the curriculum remains grounded in current industry standards. Beyond classroom instruction, this role focuses on shaping the professional character of students through targeted mentorship and the modelling of ethical conduct. [What you will be working on] Deliver lectures, conduct tutorials, and facilitate discussions for pre-hospital emergency care modules at diploma and advanced diploma levels. Impart theoretical knowledge with an emphasis on practical applications in both civilian and/or military contexts. Conduct practical evaluations, and assessments to measure learners’ proficiency and understanding of paramedic concepts. Stay updated on the latest developments in emergency medical services and incorporate current practices and technologies into the program. Instil values of professionalism, compassion, and ethical conduct in learners. Work alongside colleagues, industry professionals, and healthcare organizations to improve the relevance of the educational experience. Maintain a commitment to personal and professional development regarding medical practices and teaching methodologies. [What we are looking for] Relevant Paramedicine qualifications. Qualifications from overseas paramedic programs will also be considered. A minimum of 5 years of experience in emergency ambulance services in Singapore, with a demonstrated understanding of real-world scenarios. Strong verbal and written communication abilities to effectively convey complex concepts and facilitate learning. Strong skills in building positive, collaborative relationships with students, colleagues, and industry professionals. An effective planner capable of sequencing learning to successfully build student knowledge and skills. The ability to serve as a role model through a high level of professionalism in appearance, conduct, and communication."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer---Senior-Lecturer--Medical-Sciences----School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000035150": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Snr Lecturer (Medical Sciences) - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] [What the role is] You will be working in the School of Health & Social Sciences to plan, develop and teach Medical Science modules such as anatomy, physiology, pharmacology and pathophysiology for Nursing, Paramedic and Oral Health Therapy learners at Diploma, Specialist Diploma and Advanced Diploma levels. [What you will be working on] Conduct lectures, tutorials, lab sessions, project supervision for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners. Plan and develop course curricula. Perform mentoring duties to assigned group of learners. Participate in committees/workgroups within NYP or with external stakeholders as assigned. Lead/co-lead overseas educational and learning programmes, immersion trips or events etc. to develop students as global citizens. [What we are looking for] At least 3 years of relevant working experience in the Singapore hospital setting as a medical officer. MBBS or equivalent qualification & recency in local clinical practice. Candidate must have current/valid SMC Registration. Analytical and meticulous individual who can think strategically and align with NYP and the national agenda. People-oriented individuals who possess strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills. Good at thinking from a human-centric perspective; working in cross-functional teams; strength in resourcing, critical thinking, sense making; taking initiative; being tenacious and persevering in ambiguous complex situations; able to organize and manage multiple tasks concurrently."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Nursing----School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000034905": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Nursing) - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working in the School of Health & Social Sciences to plan, develop and teach Nursing modules for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET). [What you will be working on] Conduct lectures, tutorials, lab sessions, project supervision for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners. Plan and develop course curricula . Supervise and assess learners in the clinical areas . Perform mentoring duties to assigned group of learners. Participate in committees/workgroups within NYP or with external stakeholders as assigned. Lead/co-lead overseas educational and learning programmes, immersion trips or events etc. to develop students as global citizens. [What we are looking for] At least 5 yrs of clinical experience with at least 2 yrs in one of the specialty areas listed . Relevant qualification in Nursing & recency in local clinical practice . Candidate must have current/valid Singapore Nursing Board (SNB) practising certificate . Analytical and meticulous individual who can think strategically and align with NYP and the national agenda. People-oriented individual who possesses strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills. Good at thinking from a human-centric perspective; working in cross-functional teams; strength in resourcing, critical thinking, sense making; taking initiative; being tenacious and persevering in ambiguous complex situations; able to organize and manage multiple tasks concurrently. ​ Candidate should possess relevant experience in one or more of the following areas: Chronic Disease Management Clinical Education Critical Care Diabetes Management & Education Endoscopy Gerontology Medical-Surgical Nephro-Urology Neuroscience Oncology Orthopaedics Paediatrics Palliative Care Perioperative Perianesthesia Radiology Simulation Based Learning"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Short-Term-Clinical-Instructor---School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000005027-1": {
      "title": "Short Term Clinical Instructor - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-10-21\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] [What the role is] We are looking for individuals to join the School of Health & Social Sciences as Short-Term Clinical Instructors. In this role, you will serve as a role model and mentor for our nursing students and is responsible for providing effective instruction, assessment and support to Nursing students during their clinical placement in hospital and community facilities. You should strive to stimulate the student's interest in all aspects of clinical practice and encourage innovative thinking and approaches to practice. [What you will be working on] Orientate students to the clinical sites including working schedule, assessment methods, and overall responsibilities. Ensure that the clinical practicum facilitates the achievement of stipulated clinical learning outcomes and provide regular feedback to the Clinical Placement Provider to improve the quality of students’ clinical experiences. Support faculty with the development and achievement of the objectives and competencies for clinical skills logbook and assessments. Identify and assign appropriate activities align to the objectives and competencies for the clinical placement to enhance student learning. Impart and enhance students’ understanding of clinical related issues. Assess student’s competency to identify strengths and address weaknesses and monitor their progress to ensure stated objectives are met. Facilitate and seek interactions with the management and other health care professionals of clinical practice sites and act as point of contact for the respective hospitals. Communicate with the clinical manager with any concerns or questions regarding student progress as soon as issues arise. Prepares the staff weekly roster and submit weekly reports to the clinical manager. Maintain student confidentiality and any other duties as assigned [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in nursing At least 3 years clinical experience in acute health care settings Current knowledge of Nursing skills, trends and issues Holds a valid RN license with Singapore Nursing Board Good grasp of computer literacy and demonstrated ability to integrate technology into the learning environment and teaching methodology Good verbal and written communication skills and a demonstrated competency to interact with people at all levels of the organization Effective presentation and demonstration skills, both theoretical and practical Strong interpersonal skills, innovative, team player Able to multi-task Evidence of a personal & professional development plan Teaching experience or qualification will be an advantage"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP/Secretary--Senior-Management-Office-_JR-10000055499": {
      "title": "Secretary (Senior Management Office)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Provide high-level administrative and secretarial support to the senior management team, ensuring smooth operations and coordination of governance-related activities. [What you will be working on] Executive Support Personal Assistant to Chairman (BOG) and two Senior Directors. Manage calendars, schedule meetings, and coordinate appointments. Handle first level enquiries from public, colleagues, students and parents. Handle confidential correspondence and documentation. Office Management Oversee the Chairman’s office space, ensuring cleanliness and operational readiness of equipment and facilities. Jointly manage Huddle’s office space with other Secretaries, including asset management and budgets. Works as a team with other Secretaries and cover each other’s duties when required. Events & Administrative Support Assist in organizing BOG-related events (e.g. lunches & visits). Support claims and asset-related matters for Chairman and Senior Directors. Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with organizational policies. [What we are looking for] Prior experience in secretarial or administrative support roles is preferred. Strong organizational, time-management skills and stakeholder management skills. High level of discretion and ability to handle confidential information. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and scheduling tools."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Sr-Lecturer--Accountancy---Finance----School-of-Business-Management_JR-10000050354": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Sr Lecturer (Accountancy & Finance) - School of Business Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We're looking for accounting professionals who are genuinely curious about where the profession is heading - not necessarily experts in AI or blockchain, but people who recognise these technologies matter and want to understand why. You'll join a team exploring what accounting education looks like when automation handles the bookkeeping, AI flags anomalies, and blockchain creates immutable audit trails. Your role isn't to have all the answers - it's to help students develop the accounting judgment that matters more when technology handles the technical execution. If you've found yourself wondering which accounting tasks will still require human expertise in five years, or if you've started experimenting with AI tools in your own practice and discovered both their potential and their limitations, you already have the mindset we're building on. [What you will be working on] Teaching accounting fundamentals with an eye toward their application in technology-enabled environments. You'll help students understand why accounting principles matter, not just how to apply them manually—because manual application increasingly isn't what employers need. Designing learning experiences where students use emerging technologies (AI, data analytics tools, automation platforms) as part of their accounting work, discovering through practice when these tools help and when human judgment remains essential. Supervising student projects that explore technology applications in accounting contexts. You'll guide students through ambiguous problems where the answer isn't in a textbook—projects that require both accounting knowledge and willingness to experiment with unfamiliar tools. Collaborating with industry partners on initiatives that explore digital transformation in accounting practice. This is learning alongside students and colleagues, not lecturing from established expertise. Coaching diverse learners across Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) programmes - from school leavers building foundations to experienced accountants updating their skills for changing practice environments. Engaging in curriculum development that keeps pace with professional evolution. You'll work with colleagues to determine which traditional content remains essential and where emerging capabilities should reshape what we teach. Contributing to outreach and student development activities that connect classroom learning with professional practice and performing academic and administrative duties as required. [What we are looking for] Accounting Credentials: Relevant qualification in Accountancy with professional certification (or progress toward certification) from recognised accounting bodies such as ISCA, ACCA, CPA Australia, or equivalent. Professional Experience: Substantive work experience in accounting contexts - financial accounting, assurance, internal controls, cost accounting, or related areas. Technology Curiosity: You don't need to be a data scientist or blockchain developer, but you should be genuinely interested in how technology is reshaping accounting work. Perhaps you've: Started experimenting with AI tools for accounting tasks and discovered interesting limitations Wondered which parts of your current role could be automated and which couldn't Found yourself in conversations about RPA, data analytics, or emerging technologies and wanted to understand more Recognised that \"this is how we've always done it\" increasingly isn't sufficient justification Learning Orientation: Comfortable navigating ambiguity and learning alongside students rather than having to be the expert in everything. When faced with unfamiliar technology, your instinct is curiosity rather than resistance. Teaching Capability: Ability to explain complex accounting concepts clearly and make connections between theory and practice. This might be formal teaching experience, training colleagues, or helping others understand accounting implications in business contexts. Digital Comfort: Proficient with digital tools for productivity and communication. If you've explored tools like Power BI, UiPath, or AI platforms, that's valuable—but more important is willingness to engage with new technologies as they emerge. Communication Skills: Ability to work effectively with young adults, adult learners, industry partners, and academic colleagues. You can translate between accounting language and everyday understanding. Collaborative Mindset: Enthusiasm for working with colleagues exploring similar questions about accounting education's future, and with industry partners navigating their own digital transformation journeys."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Senior-Lead-Executive---Centre-for-Service-Excellence_JR-10000048906": {
      "title": "Senior/Lead Executive - Centre for Service Excellence",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As a Senior/Lead Executive of Centre for Service Excellence, you will contribute to the service delivery and experience segment by ensuring our diverse stakeholder groups including current and prospective learners, industry partners and the public are provided with optimal experience in NYP. Your role will encompass implementing effective service solutions involving customer journey mapping to manage both routine and complex cases such as complaints, feedback, and quality service matters. The ideal candidate will balance strategic planning with operational efficiency, demonstrating exceptional written communication and good analytical skill to uphold NYP’s service standards and to foster positive relationships with diverse stakeholder groups. [What you will be working on] Case Management and Service Operations Manage day-to-day operations of customer service & engagement seamlessly between physical (e.g. service centre) and digital touchpoints (e.g. contact centre, live chat) to ensure satisfaction and complete the interaction process. Apply a strategic mindset coupled with resourcefulness and meticulous attention to detail, to conduct comprehensive case analyses. Perform joint case management with internal stakeholders to identify solutions for cases arising from complaints, appeals, or issues to identify systemic problems, and determine strategies to prevent future occurrences. Coordinate replies with inputs given by the internal stakeholders according to NYP and PSD SOPs and service standards. Review draft replies for cases that need to be fronted by QSM’s Office. Capture and maintain accurate records of all customer interactions in the case management system, ensuring data is current and compliant with governance policies. Provide guidance to new and existing team members through on-the-job training/support in case management system and handling of daily operations tasks and assigned admin tasks. Service Design Support & Process Improvement Contribute to mapping customer journeys across various service touchpoints and identifying pain points or inefficiencies in the current service workflow to suggest improvements to streamline the customer experience. Actively contribute insights from case management and customer interactions to enhance service delivery and experience management by the center and to help ensure customer needs are accurately reflected in the design of new services. Co-lead and collaborate with team members to standardise service processes and protocols to ensure consistency in service delivery across multiple channels. Suggest best practices to enhance process efficiency and quality.  Identify patterns in customer enquiries and service performance. Use analytics to support data-driven decision-making in suggesting areas of improvement or resource allocation adjustments. Track key service delivery metrics and conduct basic analysis of service-related data with data analytics tools such as Excel or Power BI. Conduct basic analysis of service-related data and use data to highlight service bottlenecks or areas requiring intervention. [What we are looking for] Qualifications in Business, Communications, Customer Service, or a related field. 3-5 years of experience in service operations, case management and service communication. Strong verbal and written communication skills are highly essential to manage complex, sensitive and quality service manager (QSM) related cases. Prior corporate communication and QSM experience is an advantage. Proficiency in MS Office apps and/or Power BI to contribute to data-driven service process review. Strategic, meticulous, resourceful with good organisational skills with a commitment to contribute to service innovation projects. Prior experience in working on process improvement or service design project would be an added advantage. Possess effective interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate and influence peers to drive service improvements, interact effectively with internal and external stakeholders, and maintain a cheerful personality and innovative mindset to embrace changes and contribute ideas at work. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Snr-Lead-Exec--Stud-Exp---Digital-Platforms----Stud-Dev---Alumni-Relations_JR-10000054061": {
      "title": "Snr/Lead Exec (Stud Exp & Digital Platforms) - Stud Dev & Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Lead and enhance student experience, engagement, and holistic development initiatives through digital platforms, scholarship programme, and related student engagement programmes and signature events. The role will work closely with stakeholders to design and deliver meaningful student experiences, strengthen student participation, and support students' development journey. In addition, the role will support the administration, enhancement, and optimisation of digital platforms and systems, leveraging technology, data analytics, automation, and user experience improvements to enable effective programme delivery and student engagement. [What you will be working on] Lead and support scholar-related initiatives, including scholarship engagement, development activities, and student recognition programmes. Plan, coordinate, and deliver student engagement programmes, CCA management initiatives, and signature events that foster participation, leadership development, and a vibrant campus experience. Leverage digital platforms and technology-enabled solutions to enhance programme delivery, event management, student engagement, and operational effectiveness. Serve as the product owner for the digital platforms and related student experience systems, driving platform enhancements and continuous improvement. Gather and translate business requirements into digital solutions, system enhancements, automation, dashboards, and workflows that improve student engagement and programme delivery. Collaborate with stakeholders, IT teams, and vendors to implement and maintain digital platforms, integrations, and technologies that strengthen the student experience ecosystem. Manage platform operations, administration, governance, user support, website management, CRM, event systems, and learning platforms to ensure reliable, effective, and user-centric service delivery. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Student Development, Education, Business, Communications, Events Management, Social Sciences, Information Technology, or related disciplines, with the ability to support student engagement, holistic development, scholarship initiatives, CCA activities, and programme delivery. Experience planning, coordinating, and delivering student engagement programmes, leadership development initiatives, scholarship-related activities, CCAs, experiential learning opportunities, or signature events, with a proven ability to create meaningful and impactful student experiences. Strong understanding of student engagement strategies, programme management, stakeholder engagement, and event delivery, with the ability to design and implement initiatives that strengthen student participation, development, and campus life. Experience working with students and diverse stakeholders, including internal departments, external partners, and vendors, to deliver successful programmes, activities, and events that support student growth and engagement. Proficiency in data analytics, reporting tools, Power BI, Excel, and data-driven decision-making, with the ability to monitor participation trends, evaluate programme effectiveness, generate insights, and support continuous improvement. Familiarity with digital platforms, websites, CRM systems, event management platforms, learning management systems, and student-facing applications, with the ability to support platform administration, user adoption, service delivery, and enhancement initiatives. Understanding of business analysis, process improvement, automation, Agile methodologies, design thinking, and user-centred design practices, with the ability to identify opportunities to improve programme delivery and operational effectiveness through technology. Strong stakeholder management, communication, presentation, and project coordination skills, with the ability to engage students, build partnerships, and collaborate effectively across teams to deliver meaningful student experiences and programmes. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a dynamic environment while coordinating scholarship activities, student engagement programmes, CCAs, signature events, and operational responsibilities. Interest in digital innovation, AI, automation, and emerging technologies, with the ability to leverage technology-enabled solutions to enhance student engagement, streamline operations, improve service delivery, and support holistic student development. May be required to plan, organise, and lead students on overseas immersion programmes. Experience in higher education, student development, student affairs, education technology, student systems, engagement platforms, or related environments will be an advantage, particularly in enhancing student participation, development, and overall campus experience. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Adjunct-Lecturer---Sch-of-Applied-Science_JR-10000055598": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer - Sch of Applied Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] Successful candidates will be involved in the teaching of full time (PET) and/or part time (CET) polytechnic students for various diplomas in the School of Applied Science. [What you will be working on] Successful candidates will develop course materials (where applicable) and facilitate content delivery according to syllabus, be involved in assessment preparation and marking as well as providing teaching-related administrative support. They are also expected to manage digital platforms such as the Learning Management System (LMS), execute interactive digital tools (e.g. Kahoot, Mentimeter) and conduct lessons through face-to-face and/or online modes. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Candidates should possess either one of the following qualifications or its equivalent, with relevant work experience. Biomedical/Life Sciences, Data Science degree or equivalent Chemical Engineering degree or equivalent Food Science degree or equivalent  Health Sciences, Life Sciences, Nursing degree or equivalent Those with experience in one or more of the areas listed below are preferred: Biomedical Science with Analytics At least 3 years of relevant work experience in one of more of the following areas: Clinical Laboratory Sciences (e.g. Clinical Chemistry, Blood Banking, Histopathology, Laboratory Quality Management, Clinical Laboratory Operations) Bioinformatics Database Design & Administration Predictive Analytics & Forecasting Predictive Modelling Biopharmaceutical & Chemical Engineering At least 3 years of relevant work experience in one or more of the following areas: Biologics Upstream Operations Biologics Downstream Operations Manufacturing Science and Technology Food & Beverage Business At least 8 years of relevant work experience in Western cuisine, preferably with supervisory experience in professional kitchens, fine-dining establishments, or modern restaurant operations Demonstrates a strong commitment to keeping abreast of current industry trends and developments, including sustainability practices, evolving dietary needs, and emerging culinary technologies. Demonstrates excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with proven expertise in recipe development and the ability to develop innovative culinary solutions. Pharmaceutical Science At least 3 years of relevant work experience in one or more of the following areas: Nursing / Patient Care Skills (e.g., First Aid, Phlebotomy, ECG monitoring and interpretation, Parenteral Drug Administration) Research Ethics Good Clinical Practice Clinical Trials Management AI & Data Analytics Clinical sample processing For the role related to Pharmaceutical Science, candidates with Singapore Nursing Board (SNB) registration will have an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Precision-Engineering----Sch-of-Engineering_JR-10000055557": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Precision Engineering) - Sch of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Join a collaborative team of engineering educators committed to advancing Precision Engineering and smart manufacturing education. You will design and deliver authentic learning experiences in Precision Machining, CAD, Metrology, and Industry 4.0, bridging real-world applications with classroom practice. You will also lead industry collaboration initiatives, mentoring learners to think critically, innovate confidently, and solve complex engineering challenges. You are an industry-engaged practitioner with a passion for emerging manufacturing technologies and a commitment to developing adaptable, future-ready engineering talent. [What you will be working on] Design, develop, and deliver curriculum for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) in areas such as Precision Machining, Computer-Aided Design (CAD), Metrology, and Industry 4.0 technologies. Lead and contribute to the development of applied R&D and industry collaboration projects, especially in CNC machining and Industry 4.0 domains. Guide and mentor learners through academic, project, and career development, including supervision of student projects. Undertake academic-related responsibilities such as lesson planning, assessment, project supervision, and student engagement Support School’s administrative and operational tasks as and when required Keep abreast of and respond to advancements in Precision Engineering landscape through active engagement with industry and professional bodies/communities. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Relevant degree qualifications in Manufacturing, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field. At least 3 years of relevant industry experience in the Manufacturing or Precision Engineering sector. Candidate should possess relevant experience in one or more of the following areas: CNC Machining (Turning and Milling) Computer-Aided Design and Manufacturing (CAD/CAM) IoT applications in Manufacturing environment Metrology and measurement systems, including use of advanced equipment (e.g., CMM, Vision Systems, 3D Scanners) Proficiency in at least one programming language (e.g., Python, Java, MSSQL) Preferably: Experience in conducting training or delivering technical courses in Precision Engineering topics Experience in sustainability applications in manufacturing Familiarity with AI-based solutions and their implementation within engineering or manufacturing contexts."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP-CIL3/Senior-Lead-Exec--Business-Analyst----Centre-for-Industry---Lifelong-Learning_JR-10000050040": {
      "title": "Senior/Lead Exec (Business Analyst) - Centre for Industry & Lifelong Learning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Business Analyst in the OpsTech team will play a crucial role in enhancing operational support and system capabilities for Continuing Education and Training (CET) programs and schools. This role involves analysing business processes, identifying areas for improvement, and implementing solutions to optimise system usage and improve effectiveness and support both ongoing Training Management System operations. [What you will be working on] Nanyang Polytechnic is seeking an experienced and motivated Senior/Lead Executive (Business Analyst) to join our Centre for Industry & Lifelong Learning (CIL3). Job Responsibilities * Provide better support to schools and CET institutes on TMS to optimise system usage and improve effectiveness. * Provide Level 1 support to address user issues, troubleshoot, and coordinate with vendors to resolve system problems * Accelerate change requests and drive enhancements in STEP to better support CET operations and ensure a more responsive system. * Conduct impact analysis on service requests for data patches or change requests. * Assisted in execution of User Acceptance Testing (UAT) plans, coordinating with end-users, and taking charge of issue resolution * Collaborate closely with internal stakeholders (e.g., academic schools, marketing, IT) and external partners (e.g., industry representatives) to understand needs, define requirements, and translate them into practical solutions. * Enhance end-to-end course administration support, including course setup, to streamline processes and improve efficiency. * Work closely with both academic and non-academic staff to ensure smooth management of courses. * Provide general administrative support for the department and maintain proper documentation #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Job Qualifications *Qualifications in Business, Information Systems, or a related field. * Proven years of relevant experience in business analysis, project management, or related field, preferably within the education sector, public sector, or a similar environment focused on lifelong learning. * Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to interpret large datasets and translate them into clear, concise, and actionable insights. * Strong communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders at all levels. * Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced and dynamic environment. * Knowledge of the Singapore education landscape and lifelong learning initiatives will be an advantage."
    },
