    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lead-Executive--Communications----Communication---Outreach-Department_JR-10000055790": {
      "title": "Lead Executive (Communications) - Communication & Outreach Department",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a strategic web and communications professional to strengthen NYP’s brand through creative storytelling and impactful digital communications campaigns. You will manage and create content across websites and digital platforms, support external communications, and work closely with departments to shape clear and compelling narratives to enhance audience engagement and communications outcomes. [What you will be working on] Manage NYP websites, ensuring content is clear, well‑organised and user‑friendly, while improving discoverability across search engines and AI-driven platforms through SEO and GEO best practices. Work closely with stakeholders to understand their needs, identify opportunities and translate them into effective web solutions, ensuring content structure and user journeys support intended business outcomes. Implement data tracking and set performance metrics to monitor web and campaign outcomes. Conduct research and analyse audience data to uncover insights, identify trends, and inform future communications strategies. Craft compelling content through impactful copywriting and storytelling across the NYP website and digital platforms such as online articles and eDMs. Ensure all messaging is consistent, relevant to target segments, and aligned with NYP’s brand voice. Support internal and external communications efforts across NYP, including developing communications plans for departments, assisting with media enquiries, and ensuring consistent alignment with NYP's brand voice and communications strategy. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in Communications, Marketing or relevant disciplines. At least 3 to 5 years of relevant working experience in website management, content creation, communications, or marketing communications. Experience in website content management, with a good understanding of content structure and SEO fundamentals to enhance user experience, discoverability, and engagement. Knowledge Flair for writing with the ability to craft engaging content across multiple platforms. Solid understanding of government or institutional website platforms such as Isomer, as well as understanding of SEO principles and experience using tools such as Google Analytics to guide content strategy and measure performance is an advantage. Knowledge of internal communications best practices and experience supporting departmental communications planning is an advantage. Familiarity with media relations practices, including drafting media releases, managing media enquiries, and understanding the media landscape. Skills Excellent copywriting and editing ability across a range of formats including media releases, speeches, web copy, and editorial content. Experience in content creation and editing across different formats, including written content, visuals (e.g. posters), and/or video. Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage timelines, stakeholders, and multiple priorities effectively. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with various stakeholders. Attributes Self-motivated with a strong sense of initiative, and a collaborative team player. Able to manage multiple tasks effectively, work under pressure, and meet tight deadlines. Demonstrates sound judgment, strong analytical thinking, and effective problem-solving skills to make timely and well-reasoned decisions. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Deputy-Manager-Manager---Admissions-and-Academic-Affairs-Department_JR-10000055863": {
      "title": "Deputy Manager/Manager - Admissions and Academic Affairs Department",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be leading data-driven initiatives, support strategic decision-making across student admissions and academic administration, and strengthen system capabilities. [What you will be working on] Leads and oversees a team responsible for data management, reporting and analytics, digital transformation, and systems enhancement initiatives. Partners stakeholders across the Polytechnic to leverage data, streamline operational processes, and deliver digital solutions that enhance efficiency, governance, and user experience. Manages and enhances admissions, enrolment, and academic-related systems. Lead and manage CET learners' administration operations, including offer management and academic related matters Leads and contributes to digital transformation initiatives that enhance service delivery and learners’ experience, including the development of e-workflows and process automation solutions using tools such as Microsoft Power Apps Designs and develops dashboards and reports to support admissions, enrolment, and academic operations. Leverages digital tools to generate accurate and meaningful statistics covering admissions, enrolment, academic performance, and student-related data, to analyse trends and patterns to provide actionable insights for management decision-making. Support institutional reporting requirements and data submissions to external agencies. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Analytics, Statistics, Business Analytics, or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant experience in systems administration, data management and analytics, digital transformation, or project management. Experience in leading teams in projects and engaging stakeholders across multiple functions. Proficient in data visualisation and reporting tools such as Power BI, Excel, or equivalent platforms. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate data into actionable insights. Familiarity with SQL and business process improvement methodologies, and experience in the education or public sector environment will be an added advantage. A team player with a positive attitude and strong leadership potential, with excellent stakeholder management, communication, and project management skills. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive-Senior-Executive---Eco-Campus-Solutions---Services-Dept_JR-10000055891": {
      "title": "Executive/Senior Executive - Eco-Campus Solutions & Services Dept",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Join a team of facilities management practitioners and work closely with the team on the implementation of workplace transformation efforts within the department. [What you will be working on] Contribute to the transformation strategy by supporting the team's transition towards AI adoption and digitalization efforts within ESS .   Take on the transformational AI and digitalization projects within ESS. You will work with project teams (internal/external), engage in problem-solving exercises, engage in the implementation of monitoring dashboards and be responsible for the accuracy, efficiency, explainability, performance and scalability of the AI and digitalization solutions.   Collaborate with cross-functional teams of engineers, managers and domain experts to deliver timely AI / digitalization solutions for facilities operations and space management ensuring strong documentation and record-management standards within the team.   Develop AI/digitalization solutions with service providers that enhances facilities operations and space optimization and maintain analytic tools, dashboard reporting and processes that aid in data-driven decision making.   Undertake other responsibilities as assigned to support ESS’s transformation efforts . [What we are looking for] Good interpersonal, leadership and communication (verbal & written) skills. Data analytic or relevant IT knowledge."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Sociology--Psychology---Lifeskills----Sch-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000055995": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Sociology, Psychology & Lifeskills) - Sch of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working in the School of Health & Social Sciences to plan, develop and teach sociology as the main discipline, while also contributing to the teaching of psychology and lifeskills-related modules for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET). [What you will be working on] Develop and/or conduct lessons (e.g., lectures, tutorials, seminars, project supervision, etc.) in sociology, psychology, and lifeskills-related subjects (e.g., research, critical thinking, innovation, communication, interpersonal & collaboration skills, etc.) for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners, particularly in the health and social sciences domain. Undertake assigned student mentoring, including accompanying students for overseas educational/exchange trips. Contribute to school promotional activities, administrative functions, and committee work, particularly those requiring expertise in sociology, psychology, research methods, data analysis, or social science-related fields. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Sociology, Psychology, or a closely related Social Science discipline preferably with at least 3 years of relevant work experience. Additional qualification in communication and/or other-lifeskills related competency would be an advantage as would working experience in health & social care and/or educational settings. Proficient in IT applications, including familiarity with AI tools, for administration, teaching & learning and research & data analysis. Analytical and meticulous individual who can think strategically and align with NYP and the national agenda. People-oriented individual who possesses strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills, including the capacity to work well in cross-functional teams."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP-FN/Senior-Executive---Finance-Department_JR-10000056055": {
      "title": "Senior Executive - Finance Department",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Responsible for project code setup and budgeting, preparation of financial statements, journals, and payment documentation, including grant drawdowns and internal charges. Conduct annual stocktakes and support operational and financial processes. [What you will be working on] Manage project code creation and budgeting Prepare financial statement for month-end, quarter-end, and year-end Prepare and process journals for month-end, quarter-end, and year-end including grant drawdown and internal charge Process payment documentation for NETS machine charges Conduct annual stocktakes to ensure inventory accuracy Provide other operational and financial processes #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Accounting and financial reporting knowledge Experience in journal preparation and period-end closing Budgeting and project code administration Proficient in Microsoft Excel and financial system Strong analytical, organizational, and communication skills Meticulous with good attention to detail and ability to meet deadlines"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--AI-Augmented-Product-Architect--Sch-of-Engineeering_JR-10000051317": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (AI-Augmented Product Architect)-Sch of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Nanyang Polytechnic is seeking a dynamic and experienced Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in AI-Augmented Product Architecture to contribute to our School of Engineering. This role involves teaching and mentoring students across both PET (Diploma) and CET (Adult Learning) programmes using modern pedagogical approaches, curriculum development in emerging technology domains, industry engagement, applied research, and academic administration. [What you will be working on] Instructional Delivery & Facilitation Deliver lectures, tutorials and laboratory sessions across full-time Diploma programs (PET) and adult workforce upskilling modules (CET). Adopt diversified pedagogical frameworks, including project-based learning, flipped classrooms, and blended e-learning spaces. Supervise and mentor students during final-year projects, multi-disciplinary capstone assignments, and professional internship placements, particularly in Edge AI, IoT systems, and distributed architectures. Curriculum Design & Development Design, review, and revitalize instructional resources, module structures, and assessment rubrics aligned to emerging industry practices in Edge AI and distributed systems. Embed competencies such as AI model optimization and edge analytics into curriculum delivery. Develop hands-on lab modules involving embedded AI deployment, IoT telemetry pipelines, and hardware acceleration platforms. Industry Engagement & Applied Research Establish partnerships with industry players in Edge AI, IoT, and smart infrastructure. Contribute to applied R&D and industry partnership in areas such as edge AI, digital twin systems can smart connected systems. Translate real-world deployments (e.g., edge inference, chiller optimisation, smart monitoring) into learning case studies. Student Development & Administrative Duties Mentor students in technical and career development within Edge AI and embedded systems domains. Perform academic administration duties including assessment tracking and quality assurance. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Education: Degree or Postgraduate qualification in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Systems, or related fields. Industry Experience: Minimum 3–5 years in software development, AI application development, or product engineering. (Candidate should demonstrate strong proficiency in at least 2 of the following areas)     i.    AI-Augmented Development & Low-Code/No-Code Experience with low-code/no-code and AI-assisted (“vibe coding”) tools to rapidly prototype web, mobile, and backend applications.     ii.    Agentic AI & Workflow Orchestration Understanding of agentic AI concepts (reasoning, tool use, multi-step workflows) and ability to build agent-driven applications integrated with APIs or IoT systems.     iii.   LLM Deployment (Cloud & Edge) Familiarity with deploying LLMs via cloud and/or edge (SLMs), including integration into applications and trade-offs (latency, cost, privacy).     iv.   Cross-Platform Application Development Experience in building web and cross-OS mobile apps (iOS & Android) using frameworks such as Flutter or React Native, with simple, user-centric UI design.     v.    AI Application Security & Risk Awareness Awareness of risks (e.g., prompt injection, data leakage, API vulnerabilities) and basic practices in secure AI application design and governance."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP/Senior-Executive--Social-Work-_JR-10000053360": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Social Work)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working with the School of Health and Social Sciences supporting the social work section on the administrative work and also on other industry-related work. [What you will be working on] Social Work Course advising to prospective learners Social Media marketing of courses Lead or support in school-level or course-related events such as pre-placement workshops, orientation programme, Open House activities, Alumni events, Overseas Student exchanges and Study Trips Support and maintain course and placement database Support administration of course applications, procurement and facilities bookings [What we are looking for] Diploma in any field (preferably in Social Work or a related discipline) At least 3 years of relevant work experience, including programme and event management Good team player with strong communication and interpersonal skills Service-oriented mindset in supporting academic and operational stakeholders Ability to manage multiple operational tasks concurrently with minimal supervision Proficient in Microsoft Excel, and other Microsoft applications Strong administrative skills with a proven track record of managing administrative and procurement processes effectively"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive--CET-Admin----School-of-Design---Media_JR-10000052988": {
      "title": "Executive (CET Admin) - School of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This role provides operational administrative support for the delivery of short courses under Continuing Education and Training (CET). The candidate will support course setup in the course management system, participant onboarding, attendance administration, and day-to-day course logistics to ensure each course run is delivered smoothly and accurately. Working closely with course teams and trainers, the candidate will coordinate trainer availability, manage the course calendar and room bookings, and handle on-site arrangements such as materials and refreshments. The work follows well-defined procedures, with scope to contribute to process improvements at the project level. This role is ideal for someone who is organised, detail-oriented, and enjoys keeping operations running smoothly, while building familiarity with CET administration and training funding requirements. [What you will be working on] Key Responsibilities: Set up short courses and intakes in the course management system (STEP) according to established procedures, maintaining accurate course, schedule, and trainer records, and managing the master course calendar and room bookings across runs. Process participant registration, onboarding, and enrolment confirmation, maintain participant data and supporting documents for compliance, and set up participant network access (guest WiFi) accounts where required. Administer attendance taking, tracking, and certification for each course run, and compile attendance and completion reports to support training funding and claim submissions. Coordinate refreshment ordering and venue readiness, liaising with vendors and ensuring training rooms and equipment are prepared ahead of each session. Coordinate with trainers and associate trainers to confirm availability, and process associate trainer claims and timesheets in line with established procedures. Respond to participant, trainer, and public enquiries (including MySkillsFuture), escalating non-standard cases, and administer post-course feedback surveys for funded and customised courses. Support course fee waiver requests by collating supporting documents and routing them for the required approvals. Maintain course run documents and records in the shared document system (SharePoint). [What we are looking for] Requirements: Experience in administrative or operations support, ideally within a training, education, or adult learning environment. Comfortable learning and working with structured systems and procedures, and able to pick up new course administration platforms quickly. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage attendance, records, and scheduling accurately and on time. Attention to detail in maintaining participant data and supporting documents for compliance and funding requirements. Good communication skills to liaise with participants, trainers, and vendors with tact and diplomacy. Collaborative and proactive, able to work within well-defined procedures while supporting smooth day-to-day operations. Prior experience in Continuing Education and Training (CET) administration, familiarity with SkillsFuture Singapore (SSG) funding and processes, or hands-on knowledge of the STEP course management system would be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Business-Digitalisation----School-of-Business-Management_JR-10000053797": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Business Digitalisation) – School of Business Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for professionals who can teach students how to think alongside AI tools, not just how to use them — developing adaptive analytical thinking that transfers across tools and contexts, and helping learners understand when to trust AI outputs, when to override them, and how to combine human judgment with machine capability. [What you will be working on] Design and deliver Data Analytics and Business Analytics programmes covering data literacy, data visualisation, business intelligence, predictive analytics, AI applications, and modern data platforms using tools such as Excel, Power BI, Python, and SQL. Teach predictive analytics and forecasting techniques, including machine learning, clustering, dimension reduction, and time-series analysis, using Python and industry-standard analytics libraries. Guide learners in developing data-driven solutions and lightweight application prototypes while building business analysis and project management capabilities. Integrate machine learning, generative AI, and agentic AI into teaching, enabling learners to apply AI technologies effectively, responsibly, and critically. Develop and deliver continuing education and professional development programmes that strengthen analytics and AI capabilities for working professionals. Design authentic learning activities and assessments that evaluate analytical reasoning, problem-solving, human judgment, and responsible AI usage. Develop, review, and enhance curriculum, learning materials, laboratories, and assessments, including the adoption of Python-based tools and workflows across programmes. Stay abreast of developments in analytics, AI, and emerging technologies, translating industry practices into relevant and current teaching content. Work closely with academic teams, industry partners, and stakeholders to ensure curriculum relevance and alignment with workforce needs. Provide student mentorship, pastoral care, career guidance, and internship support to nurture learners' professional growth. Participate in outreach, industry engagement, and recruitment activities to promote data literacy, analytics, AI capabilities, and the School's programmes. Support internationalisation efforts, including overseas learning programmes, study trips, and collaborative educational initiatives. Teach and engage both full-time and adult learners, adapting pedagogical approaches to diverse learner profiles and experience levels. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Data Science, Business Analytics, Statistics, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline (or Education with a strong analytics/technology focus). Minimum 3 years of relevant experience in analytics, training delivery, or professional development within technology, education, corporate, or public-sector contexts. Strong analytics capability, with experience in data preparation, analysis, modelling, and translating insights into business decisions. Proficiency in Python for analytics and machine learning, including predictive modelling, clustering, dimension reduction, forecasting, and model evaluation. Ability to develop and teach lightweight Python web applications with SQL database integration. Strong proficiency in Excel and business intelligence tools (e.g. Power BI, Tableau); exposure to modern data platforms such as Databricks is a plus. Working knowledge of machine learning, generative AI, and agentic AI, with the ability to teach concepts and guide responsible AI adoption. Familiarity with GenAI tools (e.g. ChatGPT, Claude, Microsoft Copilot) and AI ethics and governance principles. Experience with Microsoft Power Platform and Microsoft 365 technologies is an advantage. Ability to teach technical concepts to non-technical audiences and translate complex analytics and AI topics into practical learning experiences. Strong communication, stakeholder management, and collaboration skills. Relevant experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: End-to-end analytics projects, from problem framing and data preparation to analysis, visualisation, and insight communication. Designing or supervising AI-assisted or agentic analytical workflows Implementing business intelligence or automation solutions in an organisational setting Teaching or coaching with generative AI, including designing assessments that remain valid when learners have AI assistance Building a portfolio of analytics or application projects (e.g. GitHub repositories, published notebooks)"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Biologics---Process-Technology--Sch-of-Applied-Science_JR-10000054002": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Biologics & Process Technology)-Sch of Applied Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be playing an active role in the academic, professional, and personal development of the learners to prepare them for work and life. This includes development of Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) curriculums, programme delivery and working on industry projects. [What you will be working on] Develop course including curriculum development, course delivery (face-to-face & online) and project supervision. Prepare and grade assessments and supervise learners in their daily course work. Manage Learning Management System (LMS), execute interactive digital tools (e.g. Kahoot, Mentimeter) and harness technology to enhance teaching and learning. Be Personal Mentor to learners, support them in pastoral care and handle day-to-day administrative matters. Support the school’s strategic initiatives through involvement in committee work and projects. Spearhead and identify new opportunities, initiatives, and collaborations with the industry. Manage and undertake project development with industry. [What we are looking for] Highly motivated and resourceful candidates who are nurturing and enjoy interacting with learners with the following: At least 3 years of relevant work experience in biologics manufacturing related field, especially upstream and/or downstream processing . Relevant qualifications in science or chemical engineering. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Proficient in digital skills (including the use of AI and data analytics tools), ability to adapt and multi-task. Candidates are also expected to be involved in the teaching and curriculum development of areas such as: Biologics Upstream or Downstream Operations AI or Digital Skills for Process Industry Data & Statistical Methods It will be an advantage if the candidates have relevant experience and are proficient in analytics tools (e.g. Microsoft Power BI, Tableau). #LI-Hybrid"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Sr-Lecturer--Supply-Chain---Logistics-Mgt----Sch-of-Business-Mgt_JR-10000051056": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Supply Chain & Logistics Management) - Sch of Business Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Business Management is seeking a Lecturer in Supply Chain & Logistics Management. This position is responsible for developing and delivering comprehensive Diploma and Specialist Diploma programmes, focusing on areas such as supply chain technologies, AI adoption, data analytics, sustainability, freight management and purchasing. Furthermore, the Lecturer will actively manage and coordinate learners’ activities and industry-based projects. [What you will be working on] Plan, develop, and deliver learning units within the Supply Chain and Logistics curriculum, including conducting assessments, maintaining academic standards, and adopting innovative pedagogical methods. Review and update course content to maintain alignment with current supply chain industry trends, technologies, and best practices. Organise and lead company visits for the learners to acquire industry best practices. Plan and conduct immersive overseas learning journeys to cultivate global competencies and expose learners to international business & supply chain operations. Partner with industry partners to solicit feedback on learning unit content and outcomes to create a jointly developed curriculum that maximises learning. Cultivate partnerships with industry stakeholders to collaborate on training initiatives, curriculum development, and professional networking events that benefit learners and the institution. Provide guidance on academic performance, career planning, and overall well-being for the learners throughout their diploma journey. Perform administrative duties related to academic matters, departmental operations, and general administrative support. Support any section projects and ad-hoc assignments when needed. [What we are looking for] Candidates should have at least three to five years of experience across various supply chain domains and have the experience in using relevant AI tools and technology for supply chain management. Able to deliver engaging lessons in various supply chain areas such as generative AI tools in supply chain management, inventory and warehouse management, supply chain analytics, sustainability in supply chain, international freight and trade management. Skilful in leading and guiding learners through hands-on activities and projects. Strong, established networks and relationships within the relevant industry or related sectors. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with a demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective working relationships across all organisational levels. Possess sound planning, organising and multi-tasking skills, with a strong sense of responsibility for completing assigned duties on time."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive-Senior-Executive--CET----School-of-Engineering_JR-10000050980": {
      "title": "Executive/Senior Executive (CET) - School of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The individual will play a key role in leading and supporting the operations of Continuing Education & Training (CET) programmes within the School of Engineering. [What you will be working on] Liaise with Course Leads to facilitate the contextualization of training materials based on course objectives and learner profiles, ensuring alignment with CET delivery requirements. Plan and implement end-to-end CET programme delivery with minimal supervision, including liaising with trainers, managing logistics, and ensuring compliance with funding and policy requirements. Coordinate with stakeholders on assigned CET programmes, supporting proposal preparation, collating feedback, and facilitating follow-ups to maintain service quality and responsiveness. Support CET outreach efforts by contributing to marketing activities, assisting in event preparation, and participating in learner engagement initiatives under the guidance of the CET leadership team. Drive the school’s effective use of the Skills Training and Enhancement Portal (STEP), acting as a resource person to colleagues. Oversee and optimise the use of CET training facilities and digital resources, recommending improvements based on utilisation trends and learner feedback. Contribute to department-wide initiatives and cross-functional taskforces, including process reviews and data reporting exercises. Support team operations and contribute ideas to strengthen CET processes & delivery. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in Engineering field and/or training, with a preference for candidates with experience in Engineering and/or training. Resourcefulness, with a proven ability to juggle multiple tasks and adapt to changes. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. A team player, driven and possesses a strong customer service mindset. Good administrative and organisational ability. Analytical and have an eye for detail. Comfort in navigating ambiguous situations, with a focus on continuous improvement. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, with a strong command of Excel."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Development-Engineer-Snr-Development-Engineer--Embedded-System----School-of-Engineering_JR-10000038656": {
      "title": "Development Engineer (Embedded System) – School of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Centre of Innovation for Electronics and IoT (COI-EIoT) at Nanyang Polytechnic is seeking a Development Engineer to join our team. In this role, you will contribute to planning, designing, and developing innovative IoT-connected electronic products and systems based on customer requirements. You will have the opportunity to explore new IoT technologies, and work with industry partners to deliver successful projects. [What you will be working on] ·          Assist in planning, managing, and undertaking project development with industry partners. ·          Design and develop software solutions for IoT-connected electronic products and systems based on customer requirements. [What we are looking for] ·          Qualification in the relevant field such as Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Computer Engineering. ·          Experience in at least one programming language, such as C/C++ or Python. ·          Familiarity with embedded system design and implementation (IoT, sensors, networking). ·          Understanding of communication protocols such as SPI, I2C, TCP/IP and RS232/RS485. ·          Experience with wireless network stack such as Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, BLE, Zigbee, Cellular is a plus. This is an exciting opportunity for a development engineer looking to work in a dynamic and innovative environment. We are looking for a highly motivated and result-oriented individual who is passionate about technology and eager to learn. A senior position will be considered if you are an experienced development engineer who can bring value to our team. #LI-Hybrid"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Snr-Lead-Exec---Admissions---Academic-Affairs-Dept_JR-10000050476": {
      "title": "Snr/Lead Exec (ELP Analytics & Reporting) - Admissions & Acad Affairs Dept",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] To support outcomes monitoring, data analytics and reporting for the Enhanced Learning Pathways (ELP) framework, enabling evidence based oversight, policy refinement and reporting. The role ensures that Enhanced Learning Pathways outcomes are systematically tracked and supported by appropriate system and data structures in collaboration with the Digital Solutions & Services Department. [What you will be working on] 1. Outcomes Monitoring & Analysis Develop and maintain monitoring frameworks to track participation, progression and outcomes across Enhanced Learning Pathways. Analyse trends across pathway types, Schools and cohorts to identify risks, gaps and improvement opportunities. Support periodic and annual collation of pathway data from Schools and relevant units. 2. Reporting Prepare dashboards, reports and briefing materials for AAA management and senior leadership. Support governance‑level reporting by translating data into clear, decision‑ready insights. Ensure monitoring outputs are aligned with policy objectives and institutional priorities. 3. Data & Systems Enablement Work with the Digital Solutions & Services Department to define data models, data fields and system requirements for capturing Enhanced Learning Pathways information. Ensure ELP‑related data is embedded at source systems to minimise manual tracking and reconciliation. Collaborate with AAA Systems & Data Analytics teams to ensure consistency of data definitions and indicators. 4. Continuous Improvement Provide evidence‑based recommendations to inform refinements to policy parameters, implementation practices or system enhancements. Support longitudinal analysis of Enhanced Learning Pathways outcomes across cohorts. Contribute data insights to reviews of the Enhanced Learning Pathways framework. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications and experience in data analysis, reporting or performance monitoring in an academic or institutional context. Strong analytical skills with ability to translate data into governance‑ready insights. Ability to work effectively with technical teams and non‑technical stakeholders. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Creative-Media-Production----School-of-Design---Media_JR-10000056663": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Creative Media Production) - School of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking passionate, industry-experienced creative media professional to join the Animation, Games & Visual Effects team. You will shape future-ready learners by designing and delivering curricula in media, animation, games and visual effects, mentoring student teams, and bringing real studio practice into the classroom. You will also contribute to new and emerging programmes in digital content creation. [What you will be working on] Develop curriculum, deliver courses related to media, animation, game art, game design and visual effects Coach, mentor learners, and be involved in learner development activities Lead and facilitate in student exchanges and study trips for both online and in-person modes where practicable Assist in outreach activities for both online and in-person modes where practicable Undertake academic administration and development of online learning materials Design and deliver curriculum for PET and CET courses in media, animation, game art, game design, visual effects, digital and social media content creation, AI-assisted media production and related areas. Coach and mentor students in development and industry-based collaborative projects. Lead applied projects and industry collaborations in areas such as AI, AI agents and automated content pipelines, XR and real-time systems. Facilitate student exchanges, immersion programmes and study trips, both virtually and in person. Engage in outreach activities such as open houses, competitions, game jams and industry engagements. Develop high-quality digital and online learning content to support blended and self-paced learning. Take on academic administrative tasks, including course coordination, assessment planning and curriculum development. Collaborate with fellow educators and industry partners to improve teaching practice and curriculum design. Stay current with industry trends, design practices and pedagogy to ensure learner employability. [What we are looking for] Minimum 4 years of industry experience in applied arts, game art, game design, computer animation, visual effects, procedural effects and simulation, virtual production, real-time CG production, social media content production or media production. Relevant qualification in Applied Arts, Computer Art and Animation, Visual Effects, 3D Visualisation and Simulation, Game Art, Game Design, Technical Direction, Immersive Media and Technology, Digital Media, Communication / Mass Communication, Creative Technology or a related field. Candidates with an equivalent track record of shipped titles will also be considered. Proficiency in relevant industry software, such as Maya, Houdini, Blender, Unity, Unreal Engine, Photoshop, Illustrator, After Effects, Substance 3D Painter, ZBrush, Premiere Pro or DaVinci Resolve, and generative AI tools and workflows (e.g. ComfyUI or AI image, video and voice generation platforms). A portfolio of shipped titles or project work. Prior experience in teaching, mentoring, training or curriculum development is advantageous. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a passion for nurturing aspiring creators and developers. Able to work in a collaborative, interdisciplinary academic environment. Willingness and ability to teach across diplomas and to pick up new subject areas as programmes evolve. Expertise in: Foundation art skills, including observational drawing, painting, classical animation, colour and design, concept ideation, digital painting, illustration and sculpting. 2D and 3D asset creation, including procedural modelling and texturing. GUI and UI/UX design. Game and level design. Technical art, CG lighting and compositing, and look development. Character rigging and CG animation. Procedural effects, fluid simulation and other simulation workflows. Real-time CG production and virtual production. Motion capture. XR, mixed reality, augmented reality and virtual reality immersive media. 360-degree video production. AI-assisted image, video and audio generation, and post-production workflows. Creative coding and scripting for tool-building, automation and AI pipelines. Motion graphics and short-form video for social platforms. Creative production and project management for games, animation, VFX or content pipelines."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer---Experience-Design--Product----Sch-of-Design---Media_JR-10000056535": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer – Experience Design (Product) - Sch of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As end users become more discerning, design is no longer confined to a single product, space or interface. It is holistic, connected and experiential. We are looking for a designer with a strong background in Industrial Design or Product Design who is passionate about shaping meaningful experiences across products, services, spaces and interactions. You see products not as isolated artefacts, but as touchpoints within a broader user journey and ecosystem. [What you will be working on] In this role, you will shape the next generation of experience designers through teaching, curriculum development, student mentorship, industry collaboration and applied projects. You will bring an Industrial and Product Design lens to the Diploma in Experience Design, helping students understand how human-centred design, product innovation, emerging technologies and systems thinking come together to create cohesive and impactful experiences.   Responsibilities Conduct lessons and develop curriculum, learning resources and assessments in experience design, design research, human-centred design, design thinking, ideation, visualisation, prototyping and design development. Bring Industrial and Product Design expertise into multidisciplinary learning experiences, helping students understand products as part of broader customer and user experiences. Provide thought leadership and domain expertise in Industrial and Product Design within the broader Experience Design curriculum. Mentor and supervise students through industry projects, exhibitions, competitions and multidisciplinary collaborations involving products, services, spaces and digital experiences. Guide students in applying user-centred design principles, ergonomics, product development methodologies, materials and manufacturing knowledge within an experience design context. Lead or support industry collaborations, consultancy projects and applied research initiatives related to experience design, product innovation and emerging technologies. Keep curriculum and learning experiences current through developments in AI-assisted ideation, sustainable product systems, circular design, service-product ecosystems and emerging manufacturing technologies. Build and sustain strategic industry partnerships to support applied projects, internships, consultancy opportunities, CET initiatives and graduate employability. Support course management, academic administration, student recruitment, outreach activities and school-wide strategic initiatives. Develop, deliver and support Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and industry capability development initiatives related to experience design, product innovation and emerging design practices. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Industrial Design, Product Design or a related discipline, with at least 5 years of relevant industry experience preferred. Strong industry portfolio demonstrating successful product innovation, human-centred design and project delivery. Demonstrated experience in design research, concept generation, prototyping, testing and product development. Good understanding of materials, manufacturing processes, ergonomics and product development methodologies. Ability to work across disciplines and contribute to projects integrating products, services, spaces and digital technologies into cohesive user experiences. Strong appreciation of sustainability, inclusive design and emerging technologies. Passion for education, mentoring and nurturing the next generation of designers. Excellent communication, facilitation and project management skills. Experience in teaching, mentoring, training or leading design teams will be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer----Experience-Design--Interior----Sch-of-Design---Media_JR-10000056552": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer – (Experience Design -Interior) - Sch of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As end users become more discerning, design is no longer confined to a single space, product or interface. It is holistic, connected and experiential. We are looking for a designer with a strong background in Interior Design or Spatial Design who is passionate about creating meaningful experiences across spaces, products, services and interactions. You see spaces not merely as physical environments, but as experiences that influence how people engage, connect, navigate and interact. [What you will be working on] In this role, you will shape the next generation of experience designers through teaching, curriculum development, student mentorship, industry collaboration and applied projects. You will bring an Interior Design and Spatial Design lens to the Diploma in Experience Design, helping students understand how human-centred design, placemaking, emerging technologies and spatial storytelling come together to create memorable and meaningful experiences.   Responsibilities Conduct lessons and develop curriculum, learning resources and assessments in experience design, covering design research, human-centred design, design thinking, ideation, visualisation, prototyping and design development across products, spaces, services and interactions.  Bring Interior Design and Spatial Design expertise into multidisciplinary learning experiences, helping students understand how physical environments shape user experiences and behaviour.  Provide thought leadership and domain expertise in Interior and Spatial Design within the broader Experience Design curriculum. Guide students in applying spatial planning, user journey mapping, placemaking, environmental psychology, materiality and spatial storytelling within an experience design context.  Mentor and supervise students through industry projects, exhibitions, competitions and multidisciplinary collaborations involving spaces, products, services and digital experiences.  Lead or support industry collaborations, consultancy projects and applied research initiatives related to experience design, spatial innovation and emerging technologies.  Develop and evaluate curriculum, learning activities and assessments to ensure alignment with evolving industry practices and future design trends.  Keep curriculum and learning experiences current through developments in sustainability, inclusive design, smart environments, immersive and XR-enabled experiences, digital twins and Generative AI for design exploration. Build and sustain strategic industry partnerships to support applied projects, internships, consultancy opportunities, CET initiatives and graduate employability. Support course management, academic administration, student recruitment, outreach activities and school-wide strategic initiatives.  Develop, deliver and support Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and industry capability development initiatives related to experience design, spatial design and emerging design practices. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Interior Design, Spatial Design, Architecture or a related discipline, with at least 5 years of relevant industry experience preferred.  Strong industry portfolio demonstrating successful spatial, environmental or experiential design projects.  Demonstrated experience in the end-to-end design process, including research, concept development, spatial planning, design development, documentation, prototyping and presentation.  Strong understanding of spatial design principles, user-centred design, materiality, construction considerations and experiential environments.  Ability to connect spatial design with products, services, interactions and digital technologies to create cohesive user experiences.  Awareness of current and emerging practices in sustainable design, inclusive design, smart spaces, immersive environments and experience-led placemaking.  Passion for education, mentoring and nurturing the next generation of designers.  Excellent communication, facilitation, presentation and project management skills.  Experience in teaching, mentoring, coaching, training or leading design teams will be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Snr-Lecturer---Architecture--Design----Sch-of-Design---Media_JR-10000056521": {
      "title": "Lecturer/ Snr Lecturer – Architecture (Design) - Sch of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As the built environment becomes more complex, architecture is increasingly human-centred, technology-enabled, sustainable and responsive to changing social and environmental needs. We are looking for an architect or architectural designer with a strong background in Architecture or a related Built Environment discipline who sees architecture as part of a broader system of people, place, technology and experience. In this role, you will shape the next generation of architectural designers through teaching, curriculum development, mentorship, industry collaboration and applied projects. You will bring industry expertise to the Diploma in Architecture, helping students integrate design thinking, speculative design, emerging technologies, sustainability and project delivery to create relevant and future-ready built environments. [What you will be working on] Responsibilities: Conduct lessons and develop curriculum, learning resources and assessments in architectural design, covering design research, design thinking, ideation, visualisation, spatial planning, design development, documentation and presentation.  Guide students in applying architectural design principles, user-centred thinking, sustainability, materiality and building technologies within an integrated design process.  Bring professional practice and Built Environment expertise into learning experiences, helping students connect design intent with technical resolution, constructability and project delivery.  Mentor and supervise students through design studios, industry projects, exhibitions, competitions and multidisciplinary collaborations.  Introduce and apply emerging practices such as speculative design, generative and parametric design, Generative AI, Virtual Design and Construction (VDC) and Common Data Environments (CDE) where relevant to teaching and projects.  Lead or support industry collaborations, consultancy projects and applied research initiatives related to architecture, design innovation and emerging technologies.  Develop and evaluate curriculum, learning activities and assessments to ensure alignment with evolving professional practices, educational needs and future industry trends.  Build and sustain strategic industry partnerships to support applied projects, internships, consultancy opportunities, CET initiatives and graduate employability. Support course management, academic administration, student recruitment, outreach activities, school committees and school-wide strategic initiatives.  Develop, deliver and support Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and industry capability development initiatives related to architecture, the Built Environment and emerging design practices.  [What we are looking for] Requirements: Relevant qualification in Architecture or a related Built Environment discipline, with at least 5 years of relevant industry experience preferred.  Strong industry portfolio demonstrating architectural design capability and successful project development or delivery.  Demonstrated experience in the end-to-end architectural design process, including research, concept development, spatial planning, design development, documentation and presentation.  Strong understanding of architectural design principles, sustainability, materiality, building technologies and construction considerations.  Ability to connect design intent with technical development and integrated project delivery.  Awareness or experience in one or more emerging areas, such as speculative design, generative or parametric design using Rhino or equivalent, Generative AI in the design process, VDC or CDE.  Passion for education, mentoring and nurturing the next generation of architectural designers.  Excellent communication, facilitation, presentation and project management skills.  Ability to work independently and collaboratively within multidisciplinary teams.  Experience in teaching, mentoring, coaching, training or leading design teams will be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Senior-Asst-Asst-Manager---Planning---Risk-Management-Department_JR-10000056517": {
      "title": "Senior Asst/Asst Manager - Planning & Risk Management Department",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As a Senior Assistant/Assistant Manager in the Planning & Risk Management Department, you will play an integral role in shaping and driving Nanyang Polytechnic’s strategic and institutional planning efforts. You will work with colleagues across NYP to translate emerging trends and institutional priorities into coherent strategies and plans, monitor organisational performance, and generate insights to support management decision-making. [What you will be working on] Strategic Planning: Support the development and review of NYP’s strategic direction by analysing external trends, engaging stakeholders, assessing strategic priorities and identifying emerging opportunities and issues that may require strategic intervention. Strategy Implementation: Monitor and evaluate the implementation of NYP’s strategic priorities and workplans, and work with units to strengthen alignment between strategy, plans and outcomes. Corporate Planning & Engagement: Drive institution-level planning and engagement activities, including the annual work planning process, management retreats and townhalls. Performance Analysis: Analyse and synthesise institutional performance data to identify key insights, trends and gaps, and translate these into clear implications for leadership decision-making across strategy, risk and operations. [What we are looking for] Relevant experience in strategic planning or corporate planning. Strong analytical and critical thinking skills, with the ability to make sense of complex issues and translate them into clear insights and recommendations. Strong writing skills, with the ability to communicate complex ideas clearly and succinctly. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage and collaborate effectively with stakeholders across different levels of the organisation. Experience working in the public sector is preferred. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lead-Executive--Planning---Planning---Risk-Management-Dept_JR-10000050845": {
      "title": "Lead Executive (Planning), Planning & Risk Management Dept",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As a Lead Executive in the Planning & Risk Management Department, you will support the institution’s strategic direction by managing and analysing performance data, developing dashboards and reporting systems, and translating insights into recommendations that inform leadership decision-making. [What you will be working on] Organisational Performance Tracking and Analysis Data Management:  Manage the collection and reporting of performance data and other strategic indicators, and contribute to improving management processes, procedures, and systems. Dashboard Development:  Build and maintain dashboards and data reporting systems. Performance Analysis:  Support the analysis of performance data to ensure whole-of-institution alignment and inform leadership decision-making across strategy, risk and operations.  Event and Secretariat Support Support the organising and execution of events and/or meetings under the department’s ambit, as well as take on relevant administrative functions such as finance and procurement for the department. [What we are looking for] Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work in a team and collaborate with stakeholders, as well as work independently. Comfortable handling data and able to sense-make from a wide range of data and information. Able to crystallise key issues from the data and write in a structured manner. Prior working experience in the public sector is an advantage, but not a requirement. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Pharmaceutical-Science----Sch-of-Applied-Sc_JR-10000056448": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Pharmaceutical Science) - Sch of Applied Sc",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working in the School of Applied Science to plan, develop and teach pharmaceutical science specialised learning units for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners. [What you will be working on] Responsible for curriculum development and delivery, project supervision, assessment setting and marking for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET). Coach and mentor students and be involved in student development activities beyond the classroom. Collaborate with industry to enhance students’ learning. Participate in committees and contribute to administrative/ management tasks. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Requirements: Relevant qualification in Health Sciences, Life Sciences, Biomedical Science, Nursing, or related degree. Minimum 3 years of industry experience in clinical trials operations and coordination, particularly in the following areas: Clinical Patient Care Skills (e.g., First Aid, Phlebotomy, ECG monitoring and interpretation, Parenteral Drug Administration) Research Ethics Good Clinical Practice Clinical Trials/Project Management Registration with the Singapore Nursing Board is an added advantage. Passionate about training, mentoring and motivating youth and adult learners. Proficient in IT applications. Familiarity with data analytics and AI tools will be an added advantage. People-oriented individual with strong communication, interpersonal and presentation skills. Keen interest in developing new capabilities through projects and self-learning."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive--Admin----Student-Development---Alumni-Relations-Dept_JR-10000050406": {
      "title": "Executive (Admin) – Student Development & Alumni Relations Dept",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Admin Executive plays a key role in ensuring the smooth running of office operations within the Student Development & Alumni Relations Department. This role is responsible for day-to-day office administration, including procurement, finance processing, facilities bookings, and the management of equipment and logistics loans. The incumbent also provides secretariat support to the Director and routes enquiries from students and external parties. [What you will be working on] Perform procurement-related functions, including raising e-Cat purchases and goods receipt. Perform finance-related functions, including processing invoices and reimbursement claims, and handling student payments via Post-Secondary Education Account (PSEA) and AXS. Monitor and track expenditures, maintaining proper records and documentation. Perform facilities booking-related functions. Track fixed assets and stored items; support asset write-off and disposal. Maintain equipment and logistics (including blazers) for loan to support events and programmes. Perform front counter duties, including issuing keys, blazers, equipment, and logistics items. Route enquiries from students and external parties received via various channels. Provide secretariat support to the Director, including calendar management and meeting scheduling. Perform other ad-hoc administrative duties as assigned. [What we are looking for] Qualifications in office administration, procurement, or finance, and a minimum of 2 years of relevant experience. Good oral and written communication skills. Detail-oriented, independent, and self-motivated with good time management skills. A team player with good problem-solving and decision-making skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications (Word, PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook, etc.). #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Biomedical-Science-with-Analytics----Sch-of-Applied-Sc_JR-10000054658": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Biomedical Science with Analytics) - Sch of Applied Sc",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will play an active role in the academic, professional, and personal development of the learners to prepare them for work and life. This includes development of Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) curriculum, programme delivery and working on industry projects. [What you will be working on] Develop, deliver and review PET and CET curriculum, including face-to-face, online and blended learning. Design and develop teaching materials, assessments, applied projects and authentic learning activities that include integrating science with AI and data analytics. Prepare and grade assessments and supervise learners in their daily course work. Use the Learning Management System and interactive digital tools effectively, and harness technology to enhance learner engagement and outcomes. Serve as a Personal Mentor to learners, providing pastoral support and assisting with day-to-day academic and administrative matters. Contribute to school and diploma-level initiatives, committee work, outreach activities, curriculum reviews and quality assurance processes. Build and maintain strong partnerships with industry to lead and develop industry projects, internships and collaborative initiatives. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Highly motivated, resourceful and learner-centric candidates who are nurturing and enjoy interacting with learners with the following: Relevant qualifications in Biomedical Science/Life Sciences, with expertise in Clinical Laboratory Sciences and qualifications or experience in Bioinformatics, Data Analytics, Data Science or related disciplines. Minimum 3 years of relevant work experience in a science related field. Demonstrated experience applying AI, machine learning, predictive analytics or modelling to solve real-world biomedical, healthcare or life sciences problems. Proficient in analytics tools or programming languages such as SAS Viya, Python, SQL, Power BI or equivalent. Strong communication, interpersonal and mentoring skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively, adapt to changing needs and manage multiple priorities. Candidates are also expected to contribute to teaching and curriculum development in one or more of the following areas: Predictive Analytics & Forecasting, Predictive Modelling, Database Design & Administration, Data & Statistical methods and Applied Calculus."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Cybersecurity----School-of-Engineering_JR-10000045420": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Cybersecurity) – School of Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This is a full-time Lecturer position dedicated to delivering high-quality education in the field of cybersecurity. The role involves teaching and mentoring learners across foundational cybersecurity concepts, alongside broad-based exposure to cloud computing and software fundamentals. The successful candidate will contribute to curriculum delivery, provide academic guidance, and help learners build essential skills for technology careers. The role will also support industry-relevant student projects and collaborate with internal and external partners. [What you will be working on] The successful candidate will: Facilitate learning units covering fundamental cybersecurity concepts (threats, risk management, and basic security technologies), network security, cloud computing principles, and foundational software systems. Supervise student projects and provide academic guidance.  Develop and update training materials and student assessments.  Support curriculum reviews and academic operations. Stay current with emerging technology trends, integrate updated practices into teaching, and support industry-aligned learning initiatives. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] We are seeking a candidate who possesses: Degree in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a closely related discipline. Solid grounding in cybersecurity fundamentals, coupled with broad-based knowledge in cloud computing architecture and services, and basic software development principles. Experience or familiarity with standard security tools, cloud platforms (such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud), and common software environments. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a clear interest in teaching, guiding, and supporting learners.  Certifications (Advantage): Certifications such as CompTIA Security+, Network+, AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner, Microsoft Certified: Azure Fundamentals, or CEH."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Game-Design---Production----Sch-of-Design---Media_JR-10000056235": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Game Design & Production) - Sch of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking passionate, industry-experienced developers and engineers to join the Game Development & Technology (GDT) academic team. You will shape future-ready learners by designing and delivering technical curricula in game programming and emerging technologies, mentoring students, and driving innovation in applied projects. [What you will be working on] Responsibilities Design and deliver curriculum for diploma and/or specialist diploma PET and CET courses in game design, game production and related areas. Coach and mentor multidisciplinary student teams through the full development lifecycle, from concept and prototyping to production, playtesting and release. Model studio production practices in student projects, including milestone planning, Agile/Scrum and team leadership. Facilitate student exchanges, immersion programmes and study trips, both virtually and in person. Engage in outreach activities such as open houses, competitions, game jams and industry engagements. Develop high-quality digital and online learning content to support blended and self-paced learning. Take on academic administrative tasks, including course coordination, assessment planning and curriculum development. Collaborate with fellow educators and industry partners to improve teaching practice and curriculum design. Stay current with industry trends, design practices and pedagogy to ensure learner employability. Requirements Industry experience in game design, level or systems design, game production, or a related role. Relevant qualification in Game Design, Game Production, Game Development, Interactive Media or a related field. Candidates with an equivalent track record of shipped titles will also be considered. Working proficiency with a major real-time engine (e.g. Unity, Unreal Engine) for prototyping and design implementation. A portfolio of shipped titles or project work. Prior experience in teaching, mentoring, training or curriculum development is advantageous. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a passion for nurturing aspiring game creators. Able to work in a collaborative, interdisciplinary academic environment. [What we are looking for] Expertise in: Systems, level, economy and narrative design Game production and project management Player experience, UX and playtesting methodologies Game and player analytics, live operations and monetisation design Visual scripting and rapid prototyping (e.g. Unreal Blueprints, Unity Visual Scripting) Application of GenAI in design and production workflows"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Game-Technology----Sch-of-Design---Media_JR-10000056233": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Game Technology) - Sch of Design & Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking passionate, industry-experienced developers and engineers to join the Game Development & Technology (GDT) academic team. You will shape future-ready learners by designing and delivering technical curricula in game programming and emerging technologies, mentoring students, and driving innovation in applied projects. [What you will be working on] Responsibilities Design and deliver curriculum for diploma and/or specialist diploma PET and CET courses in game programming, software development and emerging technologies. Coach and mentor students in technical development and industry-based collaborative projects. Lead applied projects and industry collaborations in areas such as AI, XR and real-time systems. Facilitate student exchanges, immersion programmes and study trips, both virtually and in person. Engage in outreach activities such as open houses, competitions, hackathons and industry engagements. Develop high-quality digital and online learning content to support blended and self-paced learning. Take on academic administrative tasks, including course coordination, assessment planning and curriculum development. Collaborate with fellow educators and industry partners to improve teaching practice and curriculum design. Stay current with emerging technologies and pedagogical trends to ensure learner employability and industry alignment. Requirements Industry experience in game development and/or software development. Relevant qualification in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Game Development or a related field. Proficiency with a major real-time engine (e.g. Unity, Unreal Engine) and programming in C#, C++ and/or Python. Prior experience in teaching, mentoring, training or curriculum development is advantageous. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a passion for nurturing aspiring developers. Able to work in a collaborative, interdisciplinary academic environment. [What we are looking for] Expertise in: Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning and Data Science Generative AI (GenAI) and AI-assisted development Extended Reality (AR/VR/MR) Game, application and server backend development Cloud computing / DevOps Full stack web development 3D graphics programming (e.g. OpenGL, DirectX, Vulkan), including shader and compute shader programming"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Adjunct-Lecturer--HR-Tech--Digitalisation---Analytics----Sch-of-Business-Mgt_JR-10000056350": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer (HR Tech, Digitalisation & Analytics) - Sch of Business Mgt",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-11\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking experienced HR Technology, Digitalisation, and Analytics professionals to join the School of Business Management (SBM) as adjunct lecturers, designing and delivering industry-relevant programmes that equip PET and CET learners with future-ready digital HR and analytics capabilities. [What you will be working on] Deliver high-quality training in HR Technology, Digitalization, Analytics, and Automation Propose curriculum on topics such as HR data analytics, statistical techniques, data visualization, HRIS tools, AI applications, and HR automation workflows Facilitate workshops, case studies, and project-based learning for corporate and government clients Mentor learners in applying solutions [What we are looking for] Strong experience in HR Tech or HR digital projects Hands-on proficiency in HR data analytics, data visualization, and automation platforms Strong experience in using AI and AI Agents in HR work Knowledge of HRIS systems and emerging digital HR trends Excellent communication, facilitation, and curriculum design skills Experience in corporate training or adult learning preferred"
    }
  },
